counterfactuals.output:
1. A downhole tool comprising:  

   a first tool member having a lock profile;  

   a second tool member movable relative to the first tool member;  

   a locking member carried by the second tool member and movable between an engaged position, in which the locking member engages the lock profile to restrict relative movement between the first and second tool members, and a disengaged position; and  

   a pressure-responsive piston movable from an initial position, in which a support portion of the piston supports the locking member in the engaged position, to a release position, in which the support portion is displaced from the locking member such that the locking member is permitted to move toward the disengaged position,  

   wherein a first pressure event moves the pressure-responsive piston from the initial position to the release position without disengaging the locking member from the lock profile, and wherein, after the first pressure event, a subsequent pressure event causes the locking member to disengage from the lock profile, thereby permitting relative movement between the first and second tool members.
